{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"share","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncBroadcastSequence","text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsyncBroadcastSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","level":2,"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncBroadcastSequence"},{"text":" that multicasts elements to multiple consumers concurrently.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This operator is an alias for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"broadcast()"},{"type":"text","text":", providing identical behavior."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It enables multicasting of values from the upstream sequence to multiple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"concurrent consumers without duplicating upstream work. A consumer receives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the elements the shared sequence reads from the upstream after the consumer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"creates its iterator; elements already read and handed out are not replayed."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Example","anchor":"Example","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Create an AsyncStream that emits 3 random values between 1 and 5","let upstream = AsyncStream<Int> { continuation in","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.yield(Int.random(in: 1...5))","    continuation.finish()","}","","let sharedSequence = upstream.share()","","async let firstConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"First consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","async let secondConsumer = Task {","    for await value in sharedSequence {","        print(\"Second consumer received \\(value)\")","    }","    \/\/ prints the values the shared sequence reads after this consumer subscribed","}","","\/\/ A consumer that subscribes after the shared sequence has handed out values misses them.","await firstConsumer.value","await secondConsumer.value"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/scan\/share()"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Scan\/share()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Scan"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"share"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsyncBroadcastSequenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncBroadcastSequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ShareSequence.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/ShareSequence.swift#L113"},"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","title":"share()","modules":[{"name":"Afluent","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"extendedModule":"_Concurrency","externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrl